# Stagepass PHP boilerplate

Plain PHP 8.2 or newer. No framework. No Composer. No mail.

`api/action.php` is the only public entry. Every request names an `action`. That name is looked up in `api/actions.php` and then handed to a file in `api/actions/`. User input is never used as a file path or a function name.

A longer guide is planned at [https://stagepass.one/docs/php/](https://stagepass.one/docs/php/). That page is not live yet.

## Where to edit

Edit these:

```
api/actions.php         Allowlist: register a new action here
api/actions/*.php       Your action logic (see contact.php)
.env                    Origins, limits, APP_ENV (copy from api/.env.example)
.php/config.php         Optional PHP overrides of the .env defaults
```

Leave these alone unless you are changing the core:

```
api/action.php          Front controller
api/lib/*               Responses, request parsing, security, validation, config
```

## Layout

```
api/action.php          Public front controller (core)
api/actions.php         Action allowlist (you edit this)
api/actions/ping.php    GET health check
api/actions/contact.php POST form handler (validates only, does not send mail)
api/lib/                Shared helpers (core)
api/.env.example        Copy to the project root as .env
.php/config.php         Config outside the public api/ folder
.php/rate-limit/        Created at runtime, not public
.env                    Local environment (do not commit)
```

## Configure

1. Copy `api/.env.example` to `.env` in the project root (the folder that contains `api/`).
2. Set `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` to the exact site origins that may call this API, including the scheme and without a trailing slash. Typical values are `https://your-project.sp`, `https://your-site.webflow.io`, and `https://www.example.com`.
3. Keep `.env` out of git. On Stagepass, Caddy already returns 404 for hidden path segments such as `.env` and `.php`. On shared hosting, the document root is the folder that contains `api/` (the uploaded `dist/` contents), so the public URL stays `/api/action.php`. Deny hidden paths such as `/.env` and `/.php/` in the host config when you can.

`APP_ENV=local` turns on a hidden `boom` action used only to test error handling. Leave `APP_ENV=production` on a live host.

## Add a new action

1. Create `api/actions/newsletter.php`. The file must return a callable. Read fields with `input_string()`. Throw `ValidationException` when input is invalid (that is a 422 fail). Any other uncaught exception becomes a generic 500 error.

```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

if (!defined('STAGEPASS_PHP_ENTRY')) {
    http_response_code(404);
    exit;
}

return static function (array $input, array $config): array {
    $errors = [];
    validate_required($input, 'email', $errors);
    validate_email($input, 'email', $errors);
    if ($errors !== []) {
        throw new ValidationException($errors);
    }
    // Your logic here.
    return ['subscribed' => true];
};
```

2. Register the name in `api/actions.php`:

```php
'newsletter' => [
    'file' => 'newsletter.php',
    'methods' => ['POST'],
    'honeypot' => true,
    'rate_limit' => true,
    'origin' => 'required',
],
```

3. Call it from JavaScript with `action: 'newsletter'`. Do not add a second public PHP file unless you have a strong reason.

## Call it from JavaScript

Use the existing Stagepass loader helpers. When a local session is active, `sp.resolveLocalUrl` points at `https://your-project.sp/...`. Otherwise use the public URL of the same path on your host.

```js
const path = '/api/action.php';
const url =
  (sp.vars.isLocal && sp.resolveLocalUrl(path)) ||
  new URL(path, window.location.origin).href;

const response = await fetch(url, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    Accept: 'application/json',
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    action: 'contact',
    name: 'Ada Lovelace',
    email: 'ada@example.com',
    message: 'Hello',
    website: '', // honeypot; leave empty, hide this field in CSS
  }),
});

const result = await response.json();
// result.status is "success", "fail", or "error"
if (result.status === 'success') {
  console.log('Saved', result.data);
} else {
  console.warn(result.message, result.data);
}
```

A simple GET check:

```js
const url =
  (sp.vars.isLocal && sp.resolveLocalUrl('/api/action.php')) ||
  '/api/action.php';

const result = await fetch(url + '?action=ping', {
  headers: { Accept: 'application/json' },
}).then((r) => r.json());
```

## Response shape

Every response is JSON with `status`, `data`, and `message`, plus a matching HTTP status code.

```json
{ "status": "success", "data": { "pong": true }, "message": null }
```

```json
{
  "status": "fail",
  "data": { "email": "A valid email is required." },
  "message": "Validation failed."
}
```

```json
{
  "status": "error",
  "data": null,
  "message": "An unexpected error occurred. Try again later."
}
```

`fail` is a rejected request (validation 422, unknown action 404, wrong method 405, disallowed origin 403, too many requests 429). `error` is an unexpected server failure (500) and never includes internal details.

## Security defaults

POST actions require an `Origin` header that is on `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`. GET `ping` may omit `Origin`, but a present `Origin` still has to match the list. CORS headers are only sent for allowed origins. A filled honeypot field (`website` by default) returns a generic success and does not run the handler. Rate limiting is per IP and action, stored as files under `.php/rate-limit/`.

## Local PHP server

From the project root (the folder that contains `api/`):

```bash
php -S 127.0.0.1:8080 -t .
```

Then: `curl 'http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/action.php?action=ping'`

On a linked Stagepass domain the same file is reached at `https://your-project.sp/api/action.php`.
